

From: Samarth Tandale <samarth.tandale@oss.qualcomm.com>

The pattern:

        x == C ? y : min (x, y)

can be simplified to min (x, y) whenever C >= upper_bound (y),
because min (C, y) == y for all values y can take.  Similarly:

        x == C ? y : max (x, y)

can be simplified to max (x, y) whenever C <= lower_bound (y).

Use ranger to query the value range of y and check the bound condition.

        PR tree-optimization/125700

